# Caddy gets and renews the certificate (ACME HTTP-01 through port 80) and holds
# the pod's bearer token on :8090. The Node server does all TLS for XMPP. Caddy's
# own https port 8443 is not published: public 8443 is Fly, going to :8090.
{
	admin off
	http_port 8080
	https_port 8443
	auto_https disable_redirects
}

https://{$XMPP_DOMAIN} {
	bind 127.0.0.1
	tls {
		issuer acme {
			dir https://acme-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory
			disable_tlsalpn_challenge
		}
	}
	respond "test XMPP service" 200
}

http:// {
	respond "test XMPP service" 200
}

# The LWS pod, behind a bearer token. Fly terminates TLS in front of this.
http://:8090 {
	handle /healthz {
		respond "ok" 200
	}
	@open not header Authorization "Bearer {$POD_TOKEN}"
	@preflight method OPTIONS
	handle @preflight {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3000
	}
	handle @open {
		header Access-Control-Allow-Origin "{header.Origin}"
		respond "token required" 401
	}
	handle {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3000 {
			header_up -Authorization
		}
	}
}
